-V40-INS-PLATE-A-001","localFeature":"actualDeck.smallHole"},"approachAxis":[0,0,-1],"approachDistanceMm":30,"installationSweep":"NOT_CLAIMED","instanceId":"PX-V40-INS-M15X3-SCREW-002","reversal":"Digital staging reversal only; no physical undo claim","segments":["align axis with the deck hole","seat head on the deck top"],"stagedStart":{"featureRef":"actualDeck.smallHole.top","instanceId":"PX-V40-INS-M15X3-SCREW-002","role":"screw","rotation":[[1,0,0],[0,-1,0],[0,0,-1]],"translationMm":[167.33953526405222,8.97255921344815,32]},"stagingOnly":true},{"anchor":{"instanceId":"PX-V40-INS-PLATE-A-001","localFeature":"actualDeck.smallHole"},"approachAxis":[0,0,-1],"approachDistanceMm":30,"installationSweep":"NOT_CLAIMED","instanceId":"PX-V40-INS-M15X3-SCREW-003","reversal":"Digital staging reversal only; no physical undo claim","segments":["align axis with the deck hole","seat head on the deck top"],"stagedStart":{"featureRef":"actualDeck.smallHole.top","instanceId":"PX-V40-INS-M15X3-SCREW-003","role":"screw","rotation":[[1,0,0],[0,-1,0],[0,0,-1]],"translationMm":[167.55762826233783,-7.99588827494239,32]},"stagingOnly":true},{"anchor":{"instanceId":"PX-V40-INS-PLATE-A-001","localFeature":"actualDeck.smallHole"},"approachAxis":[0,0,-1],"approachDistanceMm":30,"installationSweep":"NOT_CLAIMED","instanceId":"PX-V40-INS-M15X3-SCREW-004","reversal":"Digital staging reversal only; no physical undo claim","segments":["align axis with the deck hole","seat head on the deck top"],"stagedStart":{"featureRef":"actualDeck.smallHole.top","instanceId":"PX-V40-INS-M15X3-SCREW-004","role":"screw","rotation":[[1,0,0],[0,-1,0],[0,0,-1]],"translationMm":[167.63334381743405,-13.886840441239215,32]},"stagingOnly":true}],"revision":1,"runtimeAdmission":false,"scale":[1,1,1],"sourceLimitations":["M6 plate thickness 2 mm PROBABLE","Photo-supported hole positions and sharp bends are instructional approximations","Presentation frames and support correspondence are replaceable","M5 standoff blind bores and thread engagement are omitted","No engineering datum, physical fit, production tolerance or torque claim","Instructional presentation placement only; no engineering datum, measurement, interface or runtime admission","Staged approach is a nonphysical exploded presentation; no installation sweep or collision-free path is claimed","Scoped overlaps are omitted thread/bore proxy detail or approximate-hole clearance, not physical fit or engagement","Presentation-only functional approximation; not physical fit/thread depth/engagement.","M6 stock 2mm PROBABLE, approximate plate-local frames; no production datum.","Body/end contacts describe authored solids and visible source order; physical uncertainties unresolved.","Camera connector frames are presentation endpoint frames derived from observation; the adopted board proxies contain no solid connector body at these frames and the interior camera marker blocks are not connectors","Slot height, seated depth and the contact normal are presentation approximations from the V40 closeups, the official text and measured source geometry; they are not a manufacturer dimension, fit or electrical claim","The FPC ribbon is a zero-solid schematic: only its connected end frame is defined. No route, length, bend, pin map or camera OEM identity is inferred (Q-09, Q-10)","Pi5 reference STEP and the Zero drawing are guidance sources read in place from the ignored vault; no vendor geometry or pixels are published","The adopted HAT proxy is a 65 x 56 mm presentation envelope. V40 step 4 and 29 panels and the SunFounder Robot HAT V4.4 render indicate a Pi-sized board (about 85 x 56 mm) with the speaker and motor connectors toward the rear end; the proxy's outline and top-feature layout are not source-faithful. Placement uses only the mounting pattern and socket, which are unaffected","Actual HAT revision stays unresolved (Q-07); socket depth is schematic and is not a seating height. The socket and header touch at one interface plane by authored dimensions only","A declared approximate-height gap between the HAT and a standoff reflects stock height differences in authored proxies, not a measured clearance","No thread engagement, torque, fit or installation sweep is claimed","The motor proxy has no mounting bores or thread detail: each screw passes through the gearbox as a declared omitted-bore proxy overlap bounded by the screw's own shank volume, not an engagement or fit","The motor's two mounting-hole positions are not modelled; the gearbox is placed from its output shaft and flange face, and screw paths are taken from the traced Plate A flange holes","Plate A flange hole positions are photo-traced approximations; the 2 mm thickness is probable, not measured","Motor wires and leads are zero-solid schematic and are not routed; no electrical, torque or retention claim","Spring washer opening roll and nut hex roll about the screw axis are deterministic presentation gauges, not measured orientations","Hook and loop tape are zero-solid abstractions: no tape geometry, thickness or exact patch size is authored, and the allocated amounts remain unresolved (Q-11)","The battery is a tutorial envelope with no safety, capacity or voltage claim; its placement belongs to the next step","No installation sweep, adhesion or fit is claimed","The adopted battery envelope is 38 mm wide while the photo-traced slotted-flange inner gap is 35 mm; the V40 panel shows the battery snug between the tabs, so the traced gap is slightly narrow. The resulting interference is declared and bounded to at most 2 mm depth on every face, not hidden","Hook and loop tape are zero-solid; the adhesion contact is the touching top face and carries no strength, fit or safety claim","The battery is an external tutorial envelope with no capacity, voltage or safety claim; its integral lead is a zero-solid schematic","The battery lead's HAT-end connector frame is not established, so the connect operation of this step stays BLOCKED until the Robot HAT battery connector has a source-backed frame","No installation sweep or fit is claimed","The pan horn is the additive instructional revision of the supplied long double-arm horn (34 mm tip to tip, tapered arms, 7.7 mm hub, 12 attachment holes at a derived 2.1 mm pitch); V40 S08 and S13 draw a two-sided horn with screws on both sides of the hub, and the printed package shows two long double-arm horns and one single-arm horn, so pan and tilt take the double-arm and steering the single-arm. The large and small cross horns are unused spare stock. Dimensions are DERIVED to about 2 to 6 percent from penny-scaled photographs; spline form, hub recess and thread geometry are not modelled","The four deck screws sit in the traced deck holes, which agree with the derived horn hole row only to within about 0.9 mm; each screw therefore has a scoped overlap with solid horn plate beside the hole, and no screw-to-horn-hole alignment is claimed","The previous trace/source interpretation carried four holes on one side and three on the other. Current photo-supported fidelity revision 03 establishes a four/four positional pattern, constructed as mirror-image rows. Diameter remains unresolved: trace 1.4 mm; clean photo fits approximately 1.69 mm. These are instructional approximations, not engineering tolerance verification; the retained 1.4 mm bores have a declared small clearance overlap with the 1.5 mm screws.","The accepted ordered stack for this step lists the horn before the plate, which is not the physical order shown in V40; it is used for membership only","Pan zero angle and horn clocking about the hub are not established; the arm is placed symmetrically across the car as a presentation gauge","No installation sweep, thread engagement or fit is claimed"],"status":"COMPLETE","stepId":"PX-V40-STEP-08","track":"instructional-only","unit":"mm","variantId":"rpi-zero-2-w","zeroSolidInstanceIds":["PX-V40-INS-HOOK-002","PX-V40-INS-LOOP-002","PX-V40-INS-RIBBON-FPC-001"]}
